{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792397962,"nonce":"B64PxaqcWxHwzFyDyyJ+z/eH/vs=","title":"Compiler diagnostics carry a point, not a span, and some lose their position entirely","message":"`CompilationError.location` is a single line/column. The LSP has to invent a 1-character range (`lsp/src/context.rs:97-102`), so editors underline one character instead of the offending expression.\n\nSome errors have no position at all. `trace(s.nope)` on a String gives \"Cannot access field 'nope': class not registered or field do...\" at line 0 column 0, while \"Cannot find name 'undefinedThing'\" is placed correctly.\n\nNeeded: errors carry a full span (start and end), and every TAST error site passes the span of the expression it rejects.","files":null}]}